<h3>What Separates the Winners From the Rest</h3>

<p>The contractors winning at lead generation share five traits that have nothing to do with budget:</p>

<p><strong>1. They track everything.</strong> They know their cost per lead by channel, cost per acquisition by campaign, lifetime value by source, and close rate by lead type. They make decisions based on data, not gut feeling.</p>

<p><strong>2. They optimize continuously.</strong> Marketing isn't a set-it-and-forget-it activity. The top contractors review their campaigns weekly, test new approaches monthly, and overhaul their strategy quarterly.</p>

<p><strong>3. They invest in assets, not just ads.</strong> They build content libraries, review profiles, and email lists that compound in value over time. They don't just rent attention through ads. They own attention through assets.</p>

<p><strong>4. They prioritize lead quality over lead quantity.</strong> They'd rather have 50 highly qualified leads than 200 unqualified ones. They optimize for revenue, not just lead volume.</p>

<p><strong>5. They systematize what works.</strong> When they find a strategy that works, they document it, train their team, and make it repeatable. They don't rely on one person's knowledge or effort.</p>

